{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513578} {:answer/id #uuid "44f257e1-6c2d-5a7b-b95b-d1cc1c85a226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{1.587}⁡(4)≈\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513715} {:answer/id #uuid "80e8559d-f893-517b-8e0e-7cc3f3f01d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{4}⁡(\\frac{1}{3})≈1.587" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513868} {:answer/id #uuid "de29e40b-df70-5eef-a11c-b501cec6c718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{1.587}⁡(\\frac{1}{3})≈4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11bc61a1-c5df-575f-a750-df7c1b87d279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{4}⁡(1.587)≈\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513578} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d76220b-8379-56f0-b6f2-29c1efe40950" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3dd9e34f-3ee0-5a42-8a59-8773ae3a745a" :question/math-academy-id "q-66569" :question/problem "$\\sqrt[3]{4}≈1.587$ is equivalent to" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given approximation can be written using exponents as follows:\n\n$$\n{4}^{1/3}≈1.587\n$$\n\nThe logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${4}^{1/3}≈1.587$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=1.587,b=4$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the approximation $\\sqrt[3]{4}≈1.587$ is equivalent to ${log}_{4}⁡(1.587)≈\\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514456 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064187 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21af4820-89b6-5931-86ed-84ec6bc973bc" :knowledge-point/title "Converting Equations With Negative Powers From Exponential Form to Logarithmic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c27e08e-7979-5085-966a-00121afa4123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{27})=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513779} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7bb6ce-8cc7-571e-bcdb-5f8b2f8aa903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{1/27}⁡(3)=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513789} {:answer/id #uuid "af149b16-2612-571f-b52c-5eeaf58f7db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{1/3}⁡(\\frac{1}{27})=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513991} {:answer/id #uuid "e8435ee1-2262-52ef-a9f1-8810afdf0d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{1/27}⁡(3)=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514139} {:answer/id #uuid "eb25b335-5a1c-5de6-9dd1-8cde3debcc45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{3}⁡(3)=-\\frac{1}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c27e08e-7979-5085-966a-00121afa4123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{27})=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513779} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe35be8a-6cae-54e8-bb3f-35ee3a0741c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb68a7c2-cb48-5196-952e-fea6e54d1914" :question/math-academy-id "q-66572" :question/problem "${3}^{-3}=\\frac{1}{27}$ can be expressed as" :question/worked-solution "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${3}^{-3}=\\frac{1}{27}$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=\\frac{1}{27},b=3$ and $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as ${log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{1}{27})=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064186 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b514d4ef-68ad-5fd4-b802-e61ca86aec2c" :knowledge-point/title "Converting Equations With Radicals Into Logarithmic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "080d06a2-ac80-5731-a0d0-206b199bf240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{9}⁡81=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513553} {:answer/id #uuid "1f13dace-deeb-5459-8d06-c6c340fa8c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{1/2}⁡9=81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513613} {:answer/id #uuid "39829f81-a9cf-5068-bf86-ed19ab5065ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{1/9}⁡81=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513683} {:answer/id #uuid "85a1a928-ea1a-584e-b442-0719b4f51dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{2}⁡81=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513881} {:answer/id #uuid "88b82b32-8bc8-502a-8a2d-cd08fa683704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{81}⁡9=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88b82b32-8bc8-502a-8a2d-cd08fa683704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{log}_{81}⁡9=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513887} :answer-field/id #uuid "946be36d-0d7e-50b8-bc82-1c900e600018" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "79a0a9c5-85f5-5fac-9044-aee801b38acc" :question/math-academy-id "q-99475" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{81}=9$ can be expressed as" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given equation can be written using exponents as follows:\n\n$$\n{81}^{1/2}=9\n$$\n\nThe logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${81}^{1/2}=9$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=9,b=81$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the equation $\\sqrt{81}=9$ is equivalent to ${log}_{81}⁡9=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}]}
